# Use a REST client supporting .http requests. Populate tokens locally; never commit them.
@base = http://localhost:8080
@customerToken = REPLACE_LOCALLY
@adminToken = REPLACE_LOCALLY
@productId = REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_UUID
@orderId = REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_UUID
@itemId = REPLACE_WITH_ITEM_UUID
@dispositionId = REPLACE_WITH_DISPOSITION_UUID
@reviewId = REPLACE_WITH_REVIEW_UUID
@revision = 1
@workflowVersion = 1
@generation = 1
@retryVersion = 1
@productVersion = 1
@inventoryVersion = 1
# Replace keys for new operations; keep them unchanged for retries.
@createKey = example-order-001
@adminKey = example-product-001
@stockKey = example-stock-001
@cancelKey = example-cancel-001
@retryKey = example-retry-001
@shortageKey = example-shortage-001

### Readiness
GET {{base}}/health/ready

### Browser OIDC settings
GET {{base}}/auth/config

### Current identity
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Catalog
GET {{base}}/api/products?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Create a physical product (admin)
POST {{base}}/api/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"کالای نمونه","type":"PHYSICAL","priceMinor":"5000000","reason":"Initial catalog setup"}

### Add physical stock; inventory has its own version
POST {{base}}/api/admin/inventory/{{productId}}/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{stockKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedVersion":{{inventoryVersion}},"delta":5,"reason":"Warehouse goods received"}

### Create checkout; save returned order ID and versions
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{createKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"items":[{"productId":"{{productId}}","quantity":1}]}

### Current-status replay: repeat exactly the create request above with the same key
GET {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Own orders
GET {{base}}/api/orders?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Filter own orders; createdTo is exclusive
GET {{base}}/api/orders?limit=25&status=COMPLETED&createdFrom=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&createdTo=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Complete retained event history, oldest first; follow nextCursor
GET {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/events?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Aggregate operational metrics (Prometheus text, admin only)
GET {{base}}/api/admin/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Reacquire an expired checkout; inspect BASKET_CHANGED before proceeding
POST {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/checkout/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedRevision":{{revision}}}

### Explicitly confirm a changed basket using its new revision
POST {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/checkout/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedRevision":{{revision}}}

### Enter payment with the current confirmed revision
POST {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/payment
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedRevision":{{revision}}}

### Eligible cancellation before first fulfillment starts
POST {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{cancelKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedVersion":{{workflowVersion}},"reason":"Customer requests cancellation"}

### Eligible item retry; admin token for RECOVERY_COST review
POST {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/items/{{itemId}}/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{retryKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedGeneration":{{generation}},"expectedRetryVersion":{{retryVersion}},"reason":"Retry after transient recovery"}

### Item attempts
GET {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/items/{{itemId}}/attempts?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Refund obligations and confirmed amounts
GET {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/refunds?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Refund logs
GET {{base}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/refunds/{{dispositionId}}/logs?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Admin orders and review queue
GET {{base}}/api/admin/orders?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Open review cases
GET {{base}}/api/admin/manual-review?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Inspect a review case
GET {{base}}/api/admin/manual-review/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Confirm permanent paid physical shortage only after investigating the count
POST {{base}}/api/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/items/{{itemId}}/shortage
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{shortageKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedGeneration":{{generation}},"reason":"Verified warehouse count cannot fulfill this line"}

### Inspect inventory discrepancies
GET {{base}}/api/admin/inventory/{{productId}}/discrepancies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Product audit
GET {{base}}/api/admin/products/{{productId}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Update catalog values (use a fresh key for this operation)
PATCH {{base}}/api/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: example-edit-001
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedVersion":{{productVersion}},"priceMinor":"6000000","reason":"Catalog price revision"}

### Reconcile a verified actual warehouse count
POST {{base}}/api/admin/inventory/{{productId}}/reconcile
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: example-count-001
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedVersion":{{inventoryVersion}},"countedOnHand":2,"reason":"Verified warehouse physical count"}

### Deactivate a product while retaining evidence
POST {{base}}/api/admin/products/{{productId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: example-deactivate-001
Content-Type: application/json

{"expectedVersion":{{productVersion}},"reason":"Product withdrawn from new sales"}
